  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Text Cursor Rays\n\nA wordmark rises into frame and a cursor sweeps across it, throwing prismatic light rays through the letters (a 112-sample ray accumulation shader); the mark shrinks away into a frosted glass card where a word is typed, slides into place, and the headline changes to a closing line.\n\nCategory: logo-stings. Length: 8 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A logo sting where light rays sweep through the wordmark, followed by a typed announcement card.\n- A product announcement: wordmark, then a word typed into a glass card and a closing line.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The logo must stay still and crisp: the rays smear the wordmark while the cursor passes.\n- The render budget is tight: the shader takes 112 samples per pixel on a CPU renderer.\n\nVariables:\n- logo_text (string): Wordmark, default \"Lumen\"\n- typed_word (string): Typed word, default \"MOTION\"\n- rest_1 (string): Headline, rest of line 1, default \"in\"\n- rest_2 (string): Headline, line 2, default \"minutes\"\n- end_1 (string): Closing card, line 1, default \"Now available\"\n- end_2 (string): Closing card, line 2, default \"for everyone\"\n- accent (color): Typed word colour, default \"#ffffff\"\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: heygen-com/hyperframes. Licence: Apache-2.0. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Text Cursor Rays\n\n  A wordmark rises into frame and a cursor sweeps across it, throwing prismatic light rays through the letters (a 112-sample ray accumulation shader); the mark shrinks away into a frosted glass card where a word is typed, slides into place, and the headline changes to a closing line.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/bd6cff8157a1a0ed5075527e673cc4f321fe9123/registry/blocks/vfx-text-cursor/vfx-text-cursor.html\n\n  Copyright HeyGen, Inc. and the Hyperframes contributors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version\n  2.0 (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with the License. You may obtain\n  a copy of the License at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Unless required by applicable\n  law or agreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\"\n  BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the License for\n  the specific language governing permissions and limitations under the License.\n\n  Changes by usemosio/blocks: fills the host frame (the card is laid out in container units and the headline is sized to fit a vertical frame); the upstream logo and announcement copy are replaced by a placeholder wordmark (drawn on 2D canvases, with text from variables) and generic headline text; the shader is unchanged apart from GLSL ES 3.0 syntax (WebGL2); typing and the slide of the typed word are computed from the timeline time instead of timeline callbacks; the canvas is drawn at the `resolution` variable; without WebGL the effect canvas is hidden.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"vfx-text-cursor\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"8\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\": \"logo_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Wordmark\", \"description\": \"The wordmark the light rays pass through (a placeholder name).\", \"default\": \"Lumen\"},\n    {\"id\": \"typed_word\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Typed word\", \"description\": \"Typed out in the card, large, before it slides to its place.\", \"default\": \"MOTION\"},\n    {\"id\": \"rest_1\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Headline, rest of line 1\", \"default\": \"in\"},\n    {\"id\": \"rest_2\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Headline, line 2\", \"default\": \"minutes\"},\n    {\"id\": \"end_1\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Closing card, line 1\", \"default\": \"Now available\"},\n    {\"id\": \"end_2\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Closing card, line 2\", \"default\": \"for everyone\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Typed word colour\", \"default\": \"#ffffff\"},\n    {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the light-ray shader is drawn at, then scaled up. It samples 112 times per pixel, so keep it low on CPU renderers.\", \"default\": 0.5, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Text Cursor Rays</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@800;900&amp;family=Big+Shoulders+Display:wght@900&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: #000;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .vtc-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .vtc-canvas {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n        .vtc-canvas-wrap { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1; }\n        .vtc-card {\n          position: absolute;\n          left: 6.25cqw;\n          top: 6.25cqh;\n          width: 87.5cqw;\n          height: 87.5cqh;\n          border-radius: 2.9cqw;\n          background: linear-gradient(160deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.11) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0.045) 42%, rgba(255,255,255,0.018) 70%, rgba(255,255,255,0.075) 100%);\n          backdrop-filter: blur(14px) saturate(1.12);\n          -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(14px) saturate(1.12);\n          border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.17);\n          box-shadow: 0 30px 90px rgba(0,0,0,0.42), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.22);\n          transform-origin: 50% 50%;\n          z-index: 3;\n          opacity: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n        }\n        .vtc-card::before {\n          content: \"\";\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          background: radial-gradient(circle at 18% 78%, rgba(37,99,235,0.1), transparent 38%), radial-gradient(circle at 82% 22%, rgba(148,163,184,0.08), transparent 34%);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .vtc-text {\n          position: absolute;\n          z-index: 1;\n          left: 6.56cqw;\n          right: 6.56cqw;\n          top: 8.9cqh;\n          bottom: 8.9cqh;\n          margin: 0;\n          display: flex;\n          flex-direction: column;\n          align-items: center;\n          justify-content: center;\n          color: #fff;\n          font: 900 min(27cqmin, 19cqw) / 0.88 \"Inter\", \"Arial Black\", Arial, sans-serif;\n          text-align: center;\n          text-shadow: 0 24px 80px rgba(0,0,0,0.58);\n        }\n        .vtc-text > span { display: block; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .vtc-w { display: inline-block; }\n        .vtc-html {\n          position: relative;\n          margin-right: 0.08em;\n          text-align: left;\n          color: var(--vtc-accent, #ffffff);\n          font-family: \"Big Shoulders Display\", Impact, \"Arial Black\", sans-serif;\n          font-weight: 900;\n          letter-spacing: 0.015em;\n          text-transform: uppercase;\n          text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255,255,255,0.1), 0 24px 72px rgba(0,0,0,0.56);\n        }\n        .vtc-type, .vtc-caret { display: inline-block; }\n        .vtc-caret { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; opacity: 0; color: var(--vtc-accent, #ffffff); }\n        .vtc-avail { font-size: min(16.5cqmin, 10.5cqw); line-height: 0.94; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"vfx-text-cursor\" data-duration=\"8\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"vtc-clip\" class=\"vtc-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"8\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"vtc-canvas\" class=\"vtc-canvas\"></canvas>\n          <div class=\"vtc-card\" id=\"vtc-card\">\n            <h1 id=\"vtc-a\" class=\"vtc-text\">\n              <span><span class=\"vtc-w vtc-html\" id=\"vtc-html\"><span class=\"vtc-type\" id=\"vtc-type\"></span><span class=\"vtc-caret\" id=\"vtc-caret\">|</span></span> <span class=\"vtc-w vtc-sup\" id=\"vtc-rest1\"></span></span>\n              <span><span class=\"vtc-w vtc-sup\" id=\"vtc-rest2\"></span></span>\n            </h1>\n            <h2 id=\"vtc-b\" class=\"vtc-text vtc-avail\"><span id=\"vtc-end1\"></span><span id=\"vtc-end2\"></span></h2>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"vfx-text-cursor\";\n            var DUR = 8;\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"vtc-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function clampNum(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n            function rgb(value) {\n              var h = hex(value, \"#000000\").slice(1);\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255];\n            }\n            var DEFS = [{\"id\": \"logo_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Wordmark\", \"description\": \"The wordmark the light rays pass through (a placeholder name).\", \"default\": \"Lumen\"}, {\"id\": \"typed_word\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Typed word\", \"description\": \"Typed out in the card, large, before it slides to its place.\", \"default\": \"MOTION\"}, {\"id\": \"rest_1\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Headline, rest of line 1\", \"default\": \"in\"}, {\"id\": \"rest_2\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Headline, line 2\", \"default\": \"minutes\"}, {\"id\": \"end_1\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Closing card, line 1\", \"default\": \"Now available\"}, {\"id\": \"end_2\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Closing card, line 2\", \"default\": \"for everyone\"}, {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Typed word colour\", \"default\": \"#ffffff\"}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the light-ray shader is drawn at, then scaled up. It samples 112 times per pixel, so keep it low on CPU renderers.\", \"default\": 0.5, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}];\n            var V = {};\n            DEFS.forEach(function (d) {\n              var raw = vars[d.id];\n              if (d.type === \"number\") V[d.id] = clampNum(raw, d.default, d.min, d.max);\n              else if (d.type === \"color\") V[d.id] = hex(raw, d.default);\n              else if (d.type === \"boolean\") V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"boolean\" ? raw : raw === \"true\" ? true : raw === \"false\" ? false : d.default;\n              else V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"string\" ? raw.trim() : d.default;\n            });\n\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * V.resolution));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * V.resolution));\n            root.style.background = \"#000\";\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            var SANS = \"Inter, system-ui, sans-serif\";\n            var U = Math.min(W, H) / 1080;\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--vtc-accent\", V.accent);\n            // The wordmark the rays pass through: a mask (white) and a colour layer, drawn once on 2D canvases.\n            var LOGO_W = Math.min(W * 0.86, 1080 * (W >= H ? U : 1)), LOGO_H = LOGO_W * 79 / 263;\n            var LOGO_X = (W - LOGO_W) / 2, LOGO_Y = (H - LOGO_H) / 2 - 8 * U;\n            function drawLogo(ctx, mono) {\n              ctx.setTransform(cw / W, 0, 0, ch / H, 0, 0);\n              ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              var mark = LOGO_H * 0.8, mx = LOGO_X + LOGO_H * 0.1, my = LOGO_Y + (LOGO_H - mark) / 2;\n              var g = ctx.createLinearGradient(mx, my + mark, mx + mark, my);\n              g.addColorStop(0, \"#2563eb\"); g.addColorStop(1, \"#93c5fd\");\n              ctx.fillStyle = mono ? \"#fff\" : g;\n              ctx.beginPath(); ctx.roundRect(mx, my, mark, mark, mark * 0.28); ctx.fill();\n              ctx.fillStyle = mono ? \"#000\" : \"rgba(0,0,0,0.55)\";\n              ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(mx + mark * 0.55, my + mark * 0.12); ctx.lineTo(mx + mark * 0.28, my + mark * 0.54); ctx.lineTo(mx + mark * 0.5, my + mark * 0.54); ctx.lineTo(mx + mark * 0.42, my + mark * 0.88); ctx.lineTo(mx + mark * 0.74, my + mark * 0.42); ctx.lineTo(mx + mark * 0.52, my + mark * 0.42); ctx.closePath(); ctx.fill();\n              ctx.fillStyle = \"#fff\"; ctx.textBaseline = \"middle\"; ctx.textAlign = \"left\";\n              var size = LOGO_H * 0.85, tx = mx + mark + LOGO_H * 0.2, avail = LOGO_X + LOGO_W - tx;\n              ctx.font = \"800 \" + size + \"px \" + SANS;\n              var w = ctx.measureText(V.logo_text).width; if (w > avail) { size *= avail / w; ctx.font = \"800 \" + size + \"px \" + SANS; }\n              ctx.fillText(V.logo_text, tx, LOGO_Y + LOGO_H / 2);\n            }\n            var maskCanvas = document.createElement(\"canvas\"), colorCanvas = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n            maskCanvas.width = colorCanvas.width = cw; maskCanvas.height = colorCanvas.height = ch;\n            function drawLogos() { drawLogo(maskCanvas.getContext(\"2d\"), true); drawLogo(colorCanvas.getContext(\"2d\"), false); }\n            drawLogos();\n            var S = { progress: 0, logoY: 760, effectMix: 0, logoScale: 1 };\n            var card = document.getElementById(\"vtc-card\"), phraseA = document.getElementById(\"vtc-a\"), phraseB = document.getElementById(\"vtc-b\");\n            var htmlWord = document.getElementById(\"vtc-html\"), htmlType = document.getElementById(\"vtc-type\"), htmlCaret = document.getElementById(\"vtc-caret\");\n            document.getElementById(\"vtc-rest1\").textContent = V.rest_1;\n            document.getElementById(\"vtc-rest2\").textContent = V.rest_2;\n            document.getElementById(\"vtc-end1\").textContent = V.end_1;\n            document.getElementById(\"vtc-end2\").textContent = V.end_2;\n            var supporting = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll(\".vtc-sup\"));\n            var WORD = String(V.typed_word).toUpperCase();\n            htmlWord.style.width = Math.max(1.2, WORD.length * 0.445) + \"em\";\n            var canvasWrap = canvas;\n            var entryEase = function (t) { return -0.806 * t * t + 1.806 * t; };\n            // Typing and the word's slide are functions of time (no timeline callbacks), so any seek is consistent.\n            var TYPE_START = 3.15, TYPE_STEP = 0.085, HOLD = 0.25;\n            var TYPE_END = TYPE_START + (WORD.length - 1) * TYPE_STEP, SLIDE_START = TYPE_END + HOLD, SLIDE_END = SLIDE_START + 0.05;\n            var offset = null;\n            function measure() {\n              htmlType.textContent = WORD;\n              htmlCaret.style.left = \"0px\";\n              var cx = card.clientWidth / 2, cy = card.clientHeight / 2;\n              var left = htmlWord.offsetLeft + htmlType.offsetLeft + htmlType.offsetWidth / 2, top = htmlWord.offsetTop + htmlType.offsetTop + htmlType.offsetHeight / 2;\n              // #vtc-a is inset inside the card, so its origin is the card's padding box offset\n              offset = { x: cx - (phraseA.offsetLeft + left), y: cy - (phraseA.offsetTop + top) };\n            }\n            function typing(t) {\n              if (!offset) measure();\n              var idx = t < TYPE_START ? 0 : Math.min(WORD.length, Math.floor((t - TYPE_START) / TYPE_STEP) + 1);\n              htmlType.textContent = WORD.slice(0, idx);\n              htmlCaret.style.left = htmlType.offsetWidth + \"px\";\n              htmlCaret.style.opacity = t >= TYPE_START - 0.05 && idx < WORD.length ? \"1\" : \"0\";\n              var k = t <= SLIDE_START ? 0 : Math.min(1, (t - SLIDE_START) / 0.05);\n              k = 1 - Math.pow(1 - k, 2);\n              htmlWord.style.transformOrigin = \"50% 50%\";\n              htmlWord.style.transform = \"translate(\" + (offset.x * (1 - k)).toFixed(2) + \"px, \" + (offset.y * (1 - k)).toFixed(2) + \"px) scale(\" + (1.8 + (1 - 1.8) * k).toFixed(4) + \")\";\n            }\n            var fontEpoch = 0;\n            if (document.fonts && document.fonts.load) {\n              [\"900 100px Inter\", \"900 100px 'Big Shoulders Display'\", \"800 100px Inter\"].forEach(function (f) { document.fonts.load(f).then(function () { fontEpoch++; offset = null; drawLogos(); if (reupload) reupload(); if (paint) paint(tl.time()); }, function () {}); });\n            }\n            var reupload = null;\n\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"in vec2 aPos;\",\n              \"out vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"void main() { v_uv = vec2(aPos.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - aPos.y * 0.5); gl_Position = vec4(aPos, 0.0, 1.0); }\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n            var FRAGMENT = `#version 300 es\nprecision highp float;\nout vec4 outColor;\nin vec2 v_uv;\nuniform vec2 resolution;\nuniform vec2 mouse;\nuniform float logoY;\nuniform float logoScale;\nuniform float effectMix;\nuniform sampler2D src;\nuniform sampler2D colorSrc;\n\n#define PI 3.141593\n#define SAMPLES 112.0\n\nfloat hash(vec2 p) {\n  return fract(sin(dot(p, vec2(489.0, 589.0))) * 492.0) * 2.0 - 1.0;\n}\n\nfloat hash(vec3 p) {\n  return fract(sin(dot(p, vec3(489.0, 589.0, 58.0))) * 492.0) * 2.0 - 1.0;\n}\n\nvec2 hash2(vec3 p) {\n  return vec2(hash(p), hash(p + 1.0));\n}\n\nvec4 readMask(vec2 uv) {\n  if (uv.x < 0.0 || uv.x > 1.0 || uv.y < 0.0 || uv.y > 1.0) {\n    return vec4(0.0);\n  }\n  return texture(src, uv);\n}\n\nvec4 readColor(vec2 uv) {\n  if (uv.x < 0.0 || uv.x > 1.0 || uv.y < 0.0 || uv.y > 1.0) {\n    return vec4(0.0);\n  }\n  return texture(colorSrc, uv);\n}\n\nvec3 spectrum(float x) {\n  return cos((x - vec3(0.0, 0.5, 1.0)) * vec3(0.6, 1.0, 0.5) * PI);\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  // v_uv runs top-down; the shader and its flipped textures work with y up\n  vec2 vUv = vec2(v_uv.x, 1.0 - v_uv.y);\n  vec2 uv = vUv;\n  vec2 logoCenter = vec2(0.5, 0.5);\n  vec2 logoUv = (uv - logoCenter) / logoScale + logoCenter + vec2(0.0, logoY / resolution.y);\n  float mask = readMask(logoUv).r;\n  vec4 logo = readColor(logoUv);\n  vec2 p = uv * 2.0 - 1.0;\n  p.x *= resolution.x / resolution.y;\n\n  vec2 mp = mouse / resolution;\n  mp.y = 1.0 - mp.y;\n  mp = mp * 2.0 - 1.0;\n  mp.x *= resolution.x / resolution.y;\n\n  vec2 rp = p;\n  vec2 d = (mp - p) / SAMPLES;\n  float acc = 0.0;\n\n  for (float i = 0.0; i < SAMPLES; i++) {\n    rp += d;\n    rp += hash2(vec3(rp, i)) * 0.5 / SAMPLES;\n\n    vec2 uv2 = rp;\n    uv2.x /= resolution.x / resolution.y;\n    uv2 = uv2 * 0.5 + 0.5;\n    vec2 rayLogoUv = (uv2 - logoCenter) / logoScale + logoCenter + vec2(0.0, logoY / resolution.y);\n    acc += readMask(rayLogoUv).r / SAMPLES;\n  }\n\n  vec4 c = vec4(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n  c -= acc * 0.24;\n  c += vec4(spectrum(cos(acc * 4.9)), 1.0) * acc * 3.65;\n  c.rgb = max(c.rgb - 0.035, 0.0);\n  c.rgb *= 1.16;\n  float cursorX = mouse.x / resolution.x;\n  float sweep = exp(-pow((uv.x - cursorX) * 6.2, 2.0));\n  float textProximity = smoothstep(0.006, 0.34, acc);\n  float longRay = smoothstep(0.004, 0.18, acc);\n  vec3 sweepColor = vec3(0.14, 0.65, 0.85) + spectrum(cursorX * 1.8) * 0.28;\n  c.rgb += sweepColor * sweep * (0.34 + textProximity * 2.35);\n  c.rgb += spectrum(cursorX + acc * 2.0) * longRay * 0.58;\n  c.rgb += logo.rgb * acc * 1.18;\n  c.rgb += logo.rgb * sweep * mask * 0.92;\n  c.rgb *= effectMix;\n  c.rgb = mix(c.rgb, logo.rgb, smoothstep(0.02, 0.75, logo.a));\n  c.rgb += vec3(1.0) * smoothstep(0.04, 0.38, mask) * 0.12 * effectMix;\n  float grain = hash(vec3(uv.xyy + mouse.x * 0.0007));\n  float logoDust = smoothstep(0.02, 0.38, acc) + smoothstep(0.03, 0.22, mask);\n  c.rgb += grain * 0.07 * (0.42 + logoDust) * effectMix;\n  c.rgb += spectrum(grain + cursorX) * abs(grain) * 0.045 * smoothstep(0.02, 0.5, acc) * effectMix;\n  c.a = 1.0;\n  outColor = c;\n}`;\n\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { alpha: false, antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var shader = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n              gl.compileShader(shader);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(shader, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(shader) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return shader;\n            }\n            var paint = null;\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var prog = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(prog, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERTEX));\n              gl.attachShader(prog, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAGMENT));\n              gl.bindAttribLocation(prog, 0, \"aPos\");\n              gl.linkProgram(prog);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(prog, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(prog) || \"link failed\");\n              gl.useProgram(prog);\n              var quad = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, quad);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 3, -1, -1, 3]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              gl.enableVertexAttribArray(0);\n              gl.vertexAttribPointer(0, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, cw, ch);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(prog, name); }\n              function tex(unit) {\n                var t = gl.createTexture();\n                gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, t);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n              }\